    "declared_proposition": "For the endpoint-aligned terms z_k=f_hat(k)^2 exp(2*pi*i*k*N/q), nearest M-sector phase quantization gives |c_N-c_N^(M)| <= 22/(7M) sum_x |f(x)|^2.",
    "mathematical_argument": "The angular error is at most pi/M, so each chord is at most pi|z_k|/M <=22|z_k|/(7M). Sum and use Parseval: q^(-1)sum_k|f_hat(k)|^2=sum_x|f(x)|^2. For Lambda supported on [1,N], the elementary energy bound sum Lambda(n)^2<=N log(N)^2 makes the quantization error at most 22N log(N)^2/(7M). To fit 56N/log(N), it suffices that M>=ceil(11 log(N)^3/196).",
